\accoffset sets how far apart accidentals are drawn when
notes of a chord with accidentals are close to each other
on the staff. When two such notes are close, the second
accidental is moved to the left, so the two don't
overlap. \accoffset sets how much it is moved, as a
multiple of the distance between two staff lines.
The default is 1.2.
It takes one number as its argument:

\accoffset 1.5

The value is applied to all instruments, also to those
created after the command is executed, e.g. with
\insts.add.
A missing or non-numeric argument gives an error.
